# EVERY WESTON FEATURE OPTION DEFAULTS TO TRUE. Read that first, because it
# inverts how the list below should be read.
#
# In meson_options.txt at 14.0.2 the feature options are all value:true --
# backend-drm, backend-x11, backend-rdp, backend-vnc, backend-pipewire,
# backend-wayland, backend-drm-screencast-vaapi, backend-headless, renderer-gl,
# xwayland, shell-desktop, shell-fullscreen, shell-ivi, shell-kiosk,
# color-management-lcms, image-jpeg, image-webp, remoting, pipewire,
# screenshare, demo-clients, wcap-decode, resize-pool, tests. Only 'doc' and
# 'test-skip-is-failure' default false.
#
# SO DELETING A LINE FROM THE DISABLE LIST ADDS A DEPENDENCY. It does not remove
# a restriction. Without that sentence this reads as fussiness, and the instinct
# on hitting a missing feature is to delete the line that turned it off -- which
# is how weston goes from three new packages to fifteen.
#
# weston -- the reference Wayland compositor, and the first compositor Duct has
# had. Until this package exists no GTK 4 program here can draw anything: gtk4
# is built for wayland only, with its x11 and broadway backends both switched
# off, so there is no fallback path either.
#
# (Those two gtk4 flags are described in prose rather than written in meson's
# -D<option>=<value> form on purpose. tools/check-recipes.sh extracts every such
# spelling from this file -- comments included -- and validates it against THIS
# package's option list, so a neighbouring package's flag written literally here
# is reported as an option weston does not offer. The natural fix someone
# reaches for is deleting the explanation, so this note exists to prevent that.
# Writing this very warning in the literal form triggered it once already.)
#
# 14.x rather than 15.x: weston 15 adds a lua build dependency, 14 does not, and
# 14 is what Debian trixie and Arch currently ship.
SRC_URL=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/weston/-/releases/14.0.2/downloads/weston-14.0.2.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=b47216b3530da76d02a3a1acbf1846a9cd41d24caa86448f9c46f78f20b6e0ac
SRC_DIR=weston-14.0.2

# KEPT ON (all already default true; named so the intent is legible in one place)
#   backend-drm      the only backend that matters on bare metal
#   backend-headless KEEP. Nothing needs it today. It is how a GTK 4 program gets
#                    tested in CI with no GPU, which is exactly the problem this
#                    workstream and the installer both have. Do not prune it as
#                    unused -- for anyone but the end user it is the most useful
#                    flag here.
#   renderer-gl      EGL/GLES through mesa; see the mesa note below
#   shell-kiosk      one application, fullscreen, no desktop furniture, which is
#                    what a live installer wants
#   backend-default  already 'drm', which is what we want; named because the
#                    combo also offers 'auto' and a future default change would
#                    otherwise be invisible
#
# TURNED OFF, with what each one drags in:
#   backend-drm-screencast-vaapi   libva
#   backend-rdp, screenshare       freerdp -- TWO separate options, both default
#                                  true, and disabling backend-rdp alone does not
#                                  cover screenshare
#   backend-vnc                    neatvnc, and pam by its own path
#   backend-pipewire, pipewire     pipewire -- again two separate options
#   remoting                       gstreamer
#   color-management-lcms          lcms2
#   image-jpeg, image-webp         libjpeg-turbo and libwebp ARE packaged, so
#                                  these are cheap to re-enable if a shell ever
#                                  wants background images; off only because
#                                  nothing needs them
#   xwayland                       xwayland and its X libraries
#   backend-x11                    nested X11 backend, pointless with no X
#   backend-wayland                nested wayland backend, unused
#   shell-desktop, shell-fullscreen, shell-ivi   the other three shells
#   demo-clients, wcap-decode      toytoolkit demos and the capture decoder
#   tests                          test-only dependencies
#   systemd                        libsystemd. Duct has elogind and no systemd;
#                                  this option is only the service plugin --
#                                  state notify, watchdog, socket activation.
#
# TWO OPTIONS ARE ARRAYS, NOT BOOLEANS, and they are the one place in this file
# where getting it wrong is LOUD:
#   simple-clients  array, default [ 'all' ]  -> []
#   tools           array                     -> []
# -Dsimple-clients=false is REJECTED, not silently ignored. Worth stating because
# it contradicts what the rest of this recipe teaches: a misspelled or
# NONEXISTENT option name is accepted and does nothing, which is how
# -Dlauncher-libseat and -Drenderer-vulkan sat in an early draft of this list
# looking like decisions when neither option exists in 14.0.2. Wrong option name,
# silent; wrong option type, loud.
MESON_ARGS="-Dbackend-drm=true -Dbackend-headless=true -Dbackend-default=drm \
-Drenderer-gl=true -Dshell-kiosk=true \
-Dbackend-drm-screencast-vaapi=false -Dbackend-rdp=false -Dscreenshare=false \
-Dbackend-vnc=false -Dbackend-pipewire=false -Dpipewire=false -Dremoting=false \
-Dcolor-management-lcms=false -Dimage-jpeg=false -Dimage-webp=false \
-Dxwayland=false -Dbackend-x11=false -Dbackend-wayland=false \
-Dshell-desktop=false -Dshell-fullscreen=false -Dshell-ivi=false \
-Ddemo-clients=false -Dwcap-decode=false -Dsimple-clients=[] -Dtools=[] \
-Dtests=false -Dsystemd=false"

# sysconfdir IS NOT PASSED, and weston has the same self-computed shape fuse3
# does -- meson.build:43 is
#     dir_sysconf = dir_prefix / get_option('sysconfdir')
# which is join_paths by another spelling. It resolves correctly for the same
# reason: meson special-cases a /usr prefix, mapping sysconfdir to the ABSOLUTE
# /etc (mesonbuild/options.py, BUILTIN_DIR_NOPREFIX_OPTIONS), so the prefix in
# front of it is discarded. Its only consumer is pam/meson.build, which installs
# into dir_sysconf/pam.d. Checked rather than assumed, because autotools does NOT
# special-case /usr and the generic autotools stage here does need
# --sysconfdir=/etc -- the trap is real, it just lives in the other stage script.
#
# MESA IS FINE DESPITE APPEARANCES. mesa is built with glx disabled and there is
# no libGL.so, which the mesa recipe flags as a known consequence. weston does
# not care: its GL renderer uses EGL and GLES and it scans out through GBM, and
# this mesa provides all three. Only programs linking -lGL directly are affected.
#
# LIBUDEV VERSION, CHECKED BECAUSE IT LOOKS LIKE A BLOCKER AND IS NOT.
# libweston/meson.build requires dependency('libudev', version: '>= 136') and
# Duct's eudev is 3.2.14, which reads as far below it. eudev's configure.ac has
# AC_SUBST(UDEV_VERSION, 251) and libudev.pc.in carries Version: @UDEV_VERSION@,
# so the .pc advertises 251. Package version and advertised libudev version are
# deliberately different numbers.
